00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.366
Yeah, you have to wear it the whole time.

00:02:06.366 --> 00:02:07.950
And airports are so eerie.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.990
They're so weird and quiet.

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:12.890
Everything's closed, very eerie and weird.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:16.074
But it's good to be back,
it's good to be home.

00:02:16.074 --> 00:02:18.730
I was in Minnesota, so they
weren't second quarantining.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.580
But now we're doing our second quarantine

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:23.240
and I'ma do it right this time Moses.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.200
Minnesota is like they're
in a second quarantine.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.760
No they're still in
their first quarantine.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.830
Yeah, it's confusing where we are

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.420
on what quarantine-

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:36.050
No Minnesota, I don't think
they know that it exists

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.600
'cause there are a lot of
people not wearing masks.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:42.480
Yikes, it does sound
oddly tempting though.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.640
It's just like you have to travel so much

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.985
for this job when this
was still an art form.

00:02:46.985 --> 00:02:50.020
And the fact that like a quiet airport,

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:53.160
row to yourself, 'cause
most of the flights are

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.650
just like way too loud
businessmen having conversations

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:00.230
