00:05:16.354 --> 00:05:18.900
Did you really kidnap someone?

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.750
Yeah, how else was I gonna get him?

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:24.513
Um, okay, I'm sorry.

00:05:24.513 --> 00:05:27.493
Wow, this is okay, first show.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:29.933
Sorry, sir, are you okay?

00:05:30.974 --> 00:05:33.123
I've been here a while.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:38.160
I used to just have a
mustache and short hair.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.430
Isn't it, the beard is cute.

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:40.290
I think the beard's cute

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.960
sometimes he gets like little crumbs in it

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:44.336
like crackers and like dog food.

00:05:44.336 --> 00:05:46.090
He's so dramatic.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:47.677
He looks really scared.

00:05:47.677 --> 00:05:48.510
(laughs)

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:49.343
Are you okay?

00:05:49.343 --> 00:05:50.370
What's your name?

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.650
Dave.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.740
We're thinking about
changing it, I don't know.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:55.850
Jenny what?

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:58.170
Okay, honestly, I'm a
little taken aback here.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:01.350
This is incredibly illegal

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:03.420
and he seems really scared.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.020
Is anyone looking for you, Dave?

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:09.909
The chances are slim, I
live with 12 other people.

00:06:09.909 --> 00:06:11.660
They're not looking for him.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:15.790
Probably not okay, Jenny I just,

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.500
I don't really know what to say, but I-

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.183
I mean, look it's perfect.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:23.530
Look Dave and I, we do a
lot of fun things together.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:25.670
Sometimes we go for walks.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.920
Sometimes I let him like
swim in the bathtub.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:28.783
Very cute.

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:32.190
Sometimes he'll stack the shelves for me,

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:35.020
perfect every day,
perfectly stacked shelves.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:37.030
He makes me little tiny samples of food

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:38.340
if I don't want the whole thing.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:42.290
And then sometimes, he just
rings the bell for no reason.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.102
It's so weird

00:06:44.102 --> 00:06:46.770
That's a call for help.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:49.560
It's part of our sustainability reusable

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:51.850
head-bag initiative here at Jenny's.

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:54.578
Yeah, reusable I don't waste stuff.

00:06:54.578 --> 00:06:55.720
Okay.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.610
I yeah, I'm not gonna tell
you how to live your life.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:59.890
I get that everyone's going
through a really rough time,

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.500
but you gotta let him go.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.510
This is, it's bananas.

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:04.490
This is insane.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:07.510
Moses no, you know what
Moses, shame on you.

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:08.343
Shame on you right now.

00:07:08.343 --> 00:07:09.176
You know what?

00:07:09.176 --> 00:07:11.100
You got to quarantine with someone.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:13.440
You had someone there when you were scared

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:15.980
and you were feeling like
the world is gonna crush you.

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:17.600
You had someone to talk to.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.740
I didn't have anybody okay?

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:22.860
I'm like thousands, if
not millions of Americans

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:25.320
who don't have anyone to quarantine with

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:28.790
imagine that loneliness, it is so intense,

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:32.240
like not being able to
touch someone for weeks,

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:35.160
just the touch it's
like, that's all I want.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.330
And then sometimes you just
want someone to talk to you.

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:39.880
You just want someone
to be like, oh hey Jen,

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:41.960
great job cooking, your
dad's real proud of you.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.500
You're way hotter than your sister.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.230
Sometimes you just want that.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.620
He knows your dad?

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.800
You know what?

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.220
I'm gonna say this right now

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:53.257
you should be really ashamed
because we pay these people

00:07:53.257 --> 00:07:58.023
$12 an hour to risk their
lives for us, right Dave?

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:03.040
We get benefits and free
plantain chips on Thursdays.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.230
But my point is that I'm saving him.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:09.080
I am saving him, from the
capitalistic death grip

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:11.190
you find yourself in
'cause you want to get some

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:15.710
Trader Giatto's fuckin
portobello mushroom sauce

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:17.363
pamplemousse lasagna.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.730
That's exactly what I buy,

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.410
but that's beside the point.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:25.010
I just think I would just feel
more, way more comfortable

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:27.340
if we're putting this
out there, this live show

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:31.270
if Dave just decided, if
he wanted to stay or leave

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:32.840
'cause it sounds like
you kind have thing going

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:34.690
but I mean, we should just let him decide

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:36.326
Jen you have to agree on that.

00:08:36.326 --> 00:08:37.260
Okay.

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:38.093
Okay, fine.

00:08:38.093 --> 00:08:39.674
Fine.

00:08:39.674 --> 00:08:41.743
I will let Dave decide.

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:45.820
So, I'm gonna untie Dave.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:46.653
Okay?

00:08:46.653 --> 00:08:48.280
We'll see what Dave wants.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:50.180
Dave, you are free to go

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:53.330
but remember, I do have central air

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:55.010
and it is a heat wave right now

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.733
so what do you think Dave?

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.076
I heard what you said

00:09:00.076 --> 00:09:03.673
about how hard it is to find somebody.

00:09:05.594 --> 00:09:06.823
I think we all struggle.

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:09.763
Let me just say.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:12.523
Run!

00:09:13.394 --> 00:09:15.600
Oh my God, is he limping?

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:17.083
Did you hobble him?

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.150
I took away his robotics, don't worry

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:22.820
I chipped him, it'll be fine.

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.050
Dave!

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:24.970
Oh my God.

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:26.900
Oh my God Okay, so well
she's gonna chase him

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.987
with a way to small net.

00:09:28.987 --> 00:09:32.523
That was Jenny Zigrino.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:35.240
You can see her obviously on Conan

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.240
